From: Peios Package Maintainers <packages@peios.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] clang: cover multiarch ROCm resource lookup

LLVM's ordinary test fixture supplies both lib and lib64 because
CLANG_INSTALL_LIBDIR_BASENAME follows LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX.  Peios uses the
multi-component suffix /x86_64-linux-peios, so the same production lookup
correctly asks the fixture for lib/x86_64-linux-peios/amdgcn/bitcode.

Alias the Peios multiarch basename to the fixture's existing lib tree and
teach the path assertion about that basename.  This keeps the
resource-directory test exercising the actual configured lookup and does not
skip or weaken its device-library assertions.

---
 .../Inputs/rocm_resource_dir/lib/x86_64-linux-peios | 1 +
 clang/test/Driver/hip-device-libs.hip                | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 120000 clang/test/Driver/Inputs/rocm_resource_dir/lib/x86_64-linux-peios

diff --git a/clang/test/Driver/Inputs/rocm_resource_dir/lib/x86_64-linux-peios b/clang/test/Driver/Inputs/rocm_resource_dir/lib/x86_64-linux-peios
new file mode 120000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/clang/test/Driver/Inputs/rocm_resource_dir/lib/x86_64-linux-peios
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+.
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/clang/test/Driver/hip-device-libs.hip b/clang/test/Driver/hip-device-libs.hip
--- a/clang/test/Driver/hip-device-libs.hip
+++ b/clang/test/Driver/hip-device-libs.hip
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
 // ALL-NOT: error:
 // ALL: {{"[^"]*clang[^"]*"}}
 
-// RESDIR-SAME: "-mlink-builtin-bitcode" "[[DEVICELIB_DIR:[^"]+(/|\\\\)rocm_resource_dir(/|\\\\)lib(64)?(/|\\\\)amdgcn(/|\\\\).*]]ocml.bc"
+// RESDIR-SAME: "-mlink-builtin-bitcode" "[[DEVICELIB_DIR:[^"]+(/|\\\\)rocm_resource_dir(/|\\\\)lib(64|(/|\\\\)x86_64-linux-peios)?(/|\\\\)amdgcn(/|\\\\).*]]ocml.bc"
 // ROCMDIR-SAME: "-mlink-builtin-bitcode" "[[DEVICELIB_DIR:[^"]+(/|\\\\)rocm(/|\\\\)amdgcn(/|\\\\).*]]ocml.bc"
 
 // ALL-SAME: "-mlink-builtin-bitcode" "[[DEVICELIB_DIR]]ockl.bc"
-- 
2.51.0
